I tried to post this earlier, but something seems to have gone wrong.
If this appears to be a double posting, I am sorry.

Plonk descended into the dungeon.  The first five levels were rather
uneventful.  Level one only seemed to have a couple of grid bugs. Level
3 had the stairs to the mines.  2&3 both had shops but were not very
useful.  A couple of empty boxes scattered across the levels. Level 4
sounded like it had a vault, but Plonk lacked the tools to find it.

So when Plonk reached lvl 6, he was still only lvl 4.  A little
concerning, but his trusty large dog was with him. This level turned
out to be a treasure trove.  There seemed to be a ton of things to
kill.  Everything had something interesting on it too.  There was also
a general store on the level.  Plonk bought a +3 plate mail and a +3
cloak of protection.  An elf had some +2 gloves and a dwarf had some +3
shoes and a +1 hard hat.  Plonk found 5 wands on this level (4 of them
on monsters).  A wand of force bolts and bullet holes seemed like they
would be the most useful, but there was also a wand that changed the
text on the ground and a wand of light.  The fifth one seemed to do
nothing.

Plonk gained three levels on this floor of the dungeon. So it was now
time to go down again. Level 7 was another good level but nothing as
great as lvl 6.  Level 8 was Delphi and it had a horrible swarm of
bees.  No matter how many Plonk killed the bees just kept coming.
These things were hard to hit too.  Plonk would swing his sword 3 or 4
times before he hit the bee.  Plonk was trapped in a room.  Bees were
coming in from one side, he decided to run out of the other door.  But
no a green elf appeared in his way.  Plonk thought that with luck there
would only be one elf which he could kill and then flee to the next
room and up the stairs.  One slash with his sword and the elf died.
But luck was not with him,  Plonk could see two more elves.  Well the
bees are stopping and the elves seem easier to kill (at least to hit).
Plonk goes after the elves. This 2nd elf is a lot harder.  The bees
have caught up to Plonk now and the 2nd elf is still standing with the
3rd one right behind him.  Now it's trouble Plonk's HP is down to just
2!  He has no choice but to #pray.

The prayer works and Plonk is back up to full HP.  Plonk takes out the
elves and starts for the room with the stairs.  Noooo there are grey
elves now!  Ok new plan.  Go after the bees.  The elves soon reach
Plonk, but not before Plonk has killed the bees!  Hooora! Still at a
very high HP, Plonk takes on the elves kill kills them.  Plonk gains a
lvl to lvl 9.

Plonk finishes looking around Delphi.  Nothing of great interest.
Plonk's dog seems to have disappeared.  It's nowhere on this level.
The elf corpses had an assortment of items, but nothing as good as
Plonk had. Unable to find his dog, Plonk moves onward to sokoban.
Plonk goes down and finds the entrance to Sokoban in the next room.

Unfortunately, as Plonk was walking to the Sokoban stairs, Plonk falls
though a trap door.   Now Plonk is in big trouble.  This room is huge
and full of very nasty things.  Luckily the upstairs are just three
away.  Plonk runs fast and luckily only gets hit by a dagger once.

Plonk is now in another room adjacent to the Sokoban stairs.  Plonk
heads off quickly for Sokoban again but is careful to avoid the trap.
Sokoban goes extremely smoothly.  Plonk completes Sokoban and emerges
as lvl 12, with two cats, a ton of food rations and a Bag of Holding.
Plonk found a large number of rings.  One of them seems cursed (at
least both cats seem afraid of it), one of them is a +1 St, and the
others don't seem to to anything.

With this loot Plonk decides it is time to return to the mines.  Up
Plonk goes. There is little resistance on the way to the mines.  There
was finally a floating eye found.  Plonk had a little trouble killing
it, but in the end ate it's corpse and felt that strange mental acuity.


Plonk did find a couple of lamps early on and that was a good thing
now.  The mine are very dark.  Plonk decided to head straight down to
the town, in hopes that the temple would be co-aligned.  Much of the
upper levels of the mines were unexplored.

Plonk arrives in town it is the Alley Town. He quickly finds the
temple.  But there is a gaping hole in front of the door.  He found
pick axe on a dwarf lord earlier, but isn't completely sure it isn't
cursed.  Plus the guards are everywhere, so there really isn't a chance
to dig a hole in the wall.

Plonk decides to close the temple door and wait for the guards to
leave.  When they leave, Plonk kicks the door down and is able to
enter.  Oh horrors of horrors it is a Lawful temple.  Plonk knows he
needs to convert this temple, but how?

Fighting with the priest is surly a bad idea.  Plonk decided to head
down and check out the rest of the mine.  That's just when Plonk has a
very sad feeling.  Hmmmm did one of the cats die? What is wrong?!?
Plonk can only find one cat and takes the cat down.

The next level is again pitch black and Plonk's lamp dies.  Fortunately
Plonk had a 2nd lamp.  Then right before Plonk's eyes the cat suddenly
changes into a Fire Elemental!  Wow this could be good.  Plonk avoids
that trap and something clicks in Plonk's mind. What that wand of text
changing might do if used on a priest? Hmmmm it might just work.

Plonk heads back with the fire elemental.  ARGH!  Plonk stepped on a
different polymorph trap.  Plonk is now a Marilith.  Plonk's great
armor is destroyed. Well this might work better anyway.  If the priest
kills Plonk in this form he'll still have to kill Plonk in orcish form
too!

Back up to the town's temple.  The fire elemental doesn't seem
interested in attacking the priest (although it happily started taking
out the guards) ZAP.  Oh wow the priest is a floating eye now!  Plonk
throws something at it, kaboom a bolt of lightning hits Plonk and a
terrifying voice booms out.  Well Plonk is blind and has returned to
orcish form.  That's ok Plonk can attack with his sword and not worry
about the floating eye's gaze.

Plonk thinks he finds the priest/eye and strikes.  Ouch! That's hot.
Ooohhh Plonk hit fire elemental.  Where is that priest/eye?? Eventually
the blindness clears us.  The priest/eye is nowhere to be found.  Plonk
finds something to sacrifice and successfully converts the alter.

Plonk leaves his assorted potions and less than useful items on the
alter and heads back down to retrieve the luck stones.

Minesend turns out to be the Mimic of the Mines.  Plonk finds the pile
with the luck stone first, then collects the other gems.  There is
luckily a coaligned unicorn around so Plonk starts to Id the gems by
throning them to the unicorn.  Eventually Plonk finishes with all of
his gems and heads back up to the temple.

Back at the temple Plonk #offers some minor beast and is granted the
Cleaver! Plonk has some fun with this and a couple of scrolls of create
monster he found.  Now it is time to make some holy water out of all of
these useless potions.  Plonk heads for the nearest fountain and starts
#dipping.  Ooops Plonk dried up a fountain.  What's that shrill sound?


Better get back to the temple.  Eventually two hostile guards find
Plonk and are quickly eliminated.  They both make nice sacrifices.
Plonk hits the other fountain and has 7 clear potions.

Plonk drops the potions on the alter and begins the water prayer.
Plonk was a little worried at first since he had just gotten the
Cleaver, but the guard sacrifices seemed to have worked.  The prayer
goes well.

It goes too well actually.  Never before have I seen this.  I should
have written down the message.  It was something like Plonk you will
now be my hand to take all the souls. A terrible black blade appeared
on the alter.  Plonk was retorted to health and another message which I
missed (Just too excited I guess).  The water was blessed and one used
on the Bag of Holding and one used on the luckstone.  That left 5
blessed clear potions.

Plonk hangs around a little while longer to sacrifice a few more
things.  But this time it always says something like you have a hopeful
feeling.  Plonk runs out of things to kill.  Plonk breifly thought
about killing the shopkeepers, but didn't quite feel strong enough and
so headed back up to the main dungeon.

Plonk returns to lvl 9 to finish exploring it.  The first new room is a
opulent throne-room (odd that there was no indication that it existed).
 Stormbringer sucks the life out of everything in there.  The chest had
nothing useful, so plonk goes over to loot the throne.  Kick and plonk
ends up back in that horrible giant room again.  This time both stairs
are far far away.

Plonk heads for the upstairs which is slightly closer than the down
stairs.  An assortment of monsters quickly surround him.  If only he
had his armor from earlier.  Even with Stormbringer it does not go
well.  Soon Plonk is down to 5HP.  Plonk #prays.  DYWYPI

Ok I assume what happened at the alter was that Plonk was crowned.
Therefore I assume my mistake was not #offering more stuff so that he
could safely pray.  Also kicking the throne I guess wasn't that good of
an idea either especially giving the room below it.

Any comments?



